report='''# RI03C / Phase 11F — Acceptance Review

**Technical checks are complete; your usability review is pending.** Candidate **0.5.26-11f.2** runs separately with isolated data. Installed 0.5.26, production saves, credentials and paused NPCDex sync are unchanged. No installation or new YouTrack publication occurred in RI03C.

## What was verified

A fresh read-only ROM catalog contains 540 physical headers and starts with no map selected. New Bark Town prepared as one map with all eight areas, 95 records and 46 known relevant conditions. Route 29 prepared separately with two areas, 38 records and eight known conditions. Both explicit handoffs retained record identities and every asset while honoring the sync pause. Portable export/reload and backend-object reconstruction match exactly. The earlier real Violet City/Sprout Tower floor proof was reused, without another extraction or upload.

All eight New Bark areas and its parent overview now have generated location images. RI03C found and corrected an overly broad decoder check: internal material labels were treated as output filenames. Labels containing a colon are valid inside the model; unsafe actual filenames and external GLB paths remain blocked. Twenty focused rendering/portability cases pass, including four new filename cases. The original ROM and source models were not rewritten.

Two UI gaps were also corrected: an empty condition match now explains the filter and offers **Show All Content for This Item**; read-only Storage Usage/YouTrack Mapping views can close while loading, and stale results cannot replace a later menu. Save/import mutation guards remain intact.

Ten integrated packaged checks pass, retaining successful unchanged checks across harness recovery. They cover final MAPDex/NPCDex conditions/images, actual map switching and filter reset, unresolved access, nested floors, short-window footer separation, one Escape, workspace switching and normal Quit. Final Quit measured 379 ms after readiness. The final source/mirror/candidate audit passed: 1,217 application files, 148 mirrored test files, three changed JavaScript syntax checks and unchanged runtime binaries.

## Review the separate window

Use the window titled **RI03C Review — … — Isolated Data**. It opens MAPDex on New Bark Town's Player's House 1F, including its newly repaired image.

1. Inspect locations and a character's actual dialogue in MAPDex. Identity/image tools are inline beside that evidence; map setup stays in the map cog.
2. Switch to NPCDex using the header workspace selector. Inspect New Bark's locations, characters and condition strip. Click a condition and an affected item. An empty match should explain itself; **All Content** restores the item's other dialogue.
3. In NPCDex, use Tray 2's cog → **Open · Route 29**. Compare its eight conditions with New Bark's 46. Use **Open · Violet City**, expand Sprout Tower and inspect its floors.
4. Check whether the tile names, images, dialogue, scope and tool placement are useful for planning. You may make local test edits. This review profile has no credentials; do not publish or enter a token. You are assessing the tool, not claiming an in-game test passed.

## Limits to keep visible

The source still has partially interpreted native/dynamic paths: 166 unresolved condition findings in New Bark and 74 in Route 29 from MX02. Raw flag/variable IDs are retained when the ROM does not supply a trustworthy name. Static images do not simulate gameplay. The archived save's manually arranged 29 New Bark appearance records/91 points are not a one-to-one source oracle for the ROM's 24 physical placements/68 point containers; block/branch evidence matters, not equal group counts. No old save was restored or silently mapped onto this clean dataset.

One managed RDX is active at a time; other local maps currently open through Content Tools. Please include that discoverability in your review. Startup of this three-map profile is still slow: the latest native run took about 37 seconds. An earlier RI03C map switch took 6.4 seconds. These and full-map checkpoint/concurrency work remain U28/U29 acceptance items.

Prior verified live NPCD grouping, native corrections, file transfers and typed/reviewed-prose reconciliation are reused from 11D/11E. RI03C's new full-map object recovery is isolated, not another live full-map upload. No external agent or emulator was started. Actual two-ROM-build acceptance remains deferred until another build exists.

**RI03C stays open until your review is recorded. Stop before U28.** U29 retains guided live acceptance; U30 owns the production installer and current release documentation. [Detailed evidence and compatibility matrix](RI03C-Verification.json).
'''
